  "body": "There are sections, and then there are opportunities that simply don't come around twice.\r\n\r\nBordering the protected beauty of Shakespear Regional Park, this incredible landholding places nature quite literally at your doorstep. Step out from your future home and straight onto some of the Coast's most spectacular walking tracks, winding through native bush, open farmland and dramatic coastline toward both Army Bay and Okoromai Bay.\r\n\r\nHeld by the same family for decades, this is one of the final chances to secure land adjoining this extraordinary regional sanctuary. Once this is gone, there's every chance another opportunity like it may not surface for a generation.\r\nThe section itself is ready and waiting. Positioned to embrace elevation, sunshine and breathtaking surroundings, it offers the perfect platform to create something truly special. Imagine designing a home where your outlook is forever protected, where the backdrop is rolling green parkland, native birdlife and the sparkling Hauraki Gulf beyond.\r\n\r\nThe lifestyle here is what sets it apart. Morning swims, paddleboards, fishing, hiking tracks, mountain biking, picnics in the park, or simply watching the changing colours roll across the landscape. Land and sea are both right here, ready for whatever kind of day you feel like having.\r\n\r\nFor golfers, Whangaparaoa Golf Club is moments away. Gulf Harbour Marina and ferry services to the city keep Auckland within easy reach, while great schools, beaches and everyday amenities remain close by.\r\nThe vendor's motivation is very real, and the pricing now reflects a clear intention to get this sold.\r\n\r\nIf you've been waiting for something rare, private and impossible to recreate, this is your moment.\r\n\r\nOpportunities bordering protected parkland are exceptionally scarce. Opportunities like this, with the walkways literally at your boundary, are even rarer.\r\n\r\nCome walk the land, stand in the silence, and picture what life here could become.\r\n\r\nTo view the property documents copy this link into your browser : https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/6LAH",
